{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pulls/1375","id":4819556693,"node_id":"PR_kwDOOeTgGM8AAAABH0SZVQ","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1375","diff_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1375.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1375.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/issues/1375","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pulls/1375/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pulls/1375/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/issues/1375/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/statuses/9174a3ffc71cf5c7617a6c64afca0802b855f770","number":1375,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"jsonrpc: preserve integer request ID precision","user":{"login":"skosovsky","id":132824114,"node_id":"U_kgDOB-q8Mg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132824114?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/skosovsky","html_url":"https://github.com/skosovsky","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skosovsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skosovsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skosovsky/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skosovsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skosovsky/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skosovsky/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skosovsky/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skosovsky/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skosovsky/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"JSON-RPC numeric ID `9007199254740993` is decoded as `9007199254740992`. A successful server response therefore echoes a different ID, and two distinct incoming IDs can become the same internal map key. This reproduces on v1.8.0 and on main at 944ac1970ff05cf145fd5b28054d7ec5464ec550.\n\nThis change decodes envelope IDs through `json.Number` and converts them exactly to the existing int64 representation. Integral decimal/exponent forms remain supported using an exact rational conversion, with a magnitude check before allocating a rational. Fractional and out-of-int64-range wire IDs return an error instead of being truncated or overflowing.\n\nCancellation request IDs also decode as `json.Number`, so cancellation matches the preserved request ID. Metadata decoding remains unchanged. The exported `MakeID` function accepts `json.Number`; its existing float64 path is unchanged and cannot recover precision already lost by callers. Numeric `CancelledParams.RequestID` values decoded from JSON now have dynamic type `json.Number`, which is documented.\n\nTests cover request/response round trips above 2^53, signed int64 boundaries, integral decimal/exponent notation, invalid numeric IDs, and cancellation parameter decoding.\n\nValidation:\n- `go test ./...` passed.\n- Targeted regression tests with `-race` passed.\n- `go build ./...` and `git diff --check` passed.\n- A separate raw HTTP reproduction against the patched SDK returned the exact ID `9007199254740993`, and confirmed adjacent IDs remain distinct. That external harness is not included in this diff.\n- The new integer round-trip regression test failed on the unpatched checkout and passes with this change.\n- The separate MCP conformance suite was not run.\n\nNo module dependencies are added. The numeric ID representation remains limited to int64; arbitrary-precision IDs are outside this patch's scope.\n\nFixes #1376.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-11T13:53:19Z"